    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** headlining the roster as our premier play (82.11). His matchup against the soft-tossing Jacob Lopez (5.06 xERA) is the most favorable on the board, further boosted by significant park factors and a solidified spot in the heart of the order. Following closely is **Yordan Alvarez** (76.86), who despite a standard park grade, is elevated by an elite xwOBA of 0.467 and favorable wind conditions that should help him capitalize on the matchup against Blade Tidwell. In our search for stolen bases, **Caleb Durbin** (66.32) remains a high-floor asset; his strong score is driven by a highly favorable matchup against Jameson Taillon and a beneficial promotion to the #3 spot in the lineup, where his speed-to-power profile is maximized.\n\nOur roster management remains focused on leveraging platoon advantages to squeeze extra value out of the bottom half of the lineup. **Lars Nootbaar** (56.75) and **Christian Yelich** (57.13) both received double-digit bumps from our dynamic platoon projections, successfully pushing them into the \u201cStrong\u201d start category despite facing middling-to-tough arms like Gabriel Hughes and Casey Mize. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Nelson Velazquez** (53.98), who narrowly made the UTIL slot over others; while his matchup against Andrew Painter is favorable, he sits just above our marginal threshold. We are monitoring **Carson Benge** (57.62) closely, as a 31% rain risk introduces significant volatility that could render his strong matchup against Bryce Elder moot if the game is shortened. With the rest of the bench\u2014including **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Colt Keith**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Chase Meidroth**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Jacob Gonzalez**\u2014all inactive today, our strategy is to rely on the current starters to weather the heavy workload against a mixed bag of opposing pitchers.",
